      "writtenOn": "2026-09-24T09:41:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "AHEVCAssembler has the same flooding issue — its addSingleNALUnit calls onIssueFIRByAssembler() unconditionally without the !hasNoSps guard, so FIR fires on every incoming packet (rate-limited to 1/sec) before any in-band SPS/VPS arrives.\n\nSimilar check is added for AHEVCAssembler\nBug: 425785365\nTest: Manual test of VT call scenario on target device.\nFlag: EXEMPT BUGFIX\nChange-Id: I6d2c21e6b37c64a08f252333146df8fb3b40791a\n\nAH263Assembler is not affected — it has no SPS-based drop/FIR logic; its only FIR path is through the MALFORMED_PACKET return in assembleMore, not per-frame.",
      "parentUuid": "aa1f7b5b_baa16999",
